<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cercōps</span></b> , ōpis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρκωψ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A species of long-tailed apes</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Manil. 4, 664</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 14,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of a Pythagorean philosopher</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 1, 38, 107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cercōpes</span></b> ,
			um, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέρκωπες</span>, <i>a cunning</i>, <i>trickish people on the island of Pithecusa</i>, <i>changed by Jupiter into monkeys</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
				92</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
